core,code,types,ui: track job lifecycle on the lineage

Background jobs used to be invisible to resume and /tree: a registry could
either keep ids that the lineage claims are live after rollback (or vice
versa), and the agent had no durable way to learn the difference. Spawning
jobs already wrote tool results into the transcript, but the lifecycle
boundaries were not recorded, so reconciling on resume meant heuristics
(string sniffing the transcript) rather than a single source of truth.

Durable JobStarted / JobFinished markers now ride the lineage alongside
the tool results the model already sees. They stay invisible to model
context and the transcript renderer (lifecycle bookkeeping only), but
resume and /tree can now decide which registry ids are still semantically
live from one authoritative walk of the lineage. /tree kills jobs whose
spawn event rolled off the lineage; resume feeds a Notice through the
prompt queue so the model knows stale ids before it can target one.
